The fix looks correct. Let me summarize the fix:

**Problem:** When an option has multiple names/aliases (e.g., `-b, --base-url`) and a default value, the default was incorrectly applied to all alias names even when one alias was already parsed.

**Root cause:** In the `mri` method of `CAC.ts`:
1. First, defaults are set for ALL alias names of each option
2. Then, parsed values are set using only the specific name that was parsed (e.g., `--base-url` becomes `baseUrl` after camelCasing)
3. The short alias `b` still retains the default value because it was never updated

**Fix:** After setting a parsed option value, we now also set all other alias names of that option to the same value. This ensures that all aliases are synchronized when an option is explicitly provided.

The fix is minimal and targeted:
```typescript
// Also set all alias names of this option to the same value
const option = cliOptions.find(o => o.names.includes(keys[0]))
if (option) {
  for (const name of option.names) {
    if (name !== keys[0]) {
      options[name] = parsed[key]
    }
  }
}
```

